=========================================================================

bcommon is a Go library of building blocks for BSV overlay applications
that publish and verify committed records. It provides a deterministic
CBOR codec, RFC 6962 Merkle roots, store references and manifests, BRC-42
key derivation under BRC-43 names with tagged PushDrop outputs, a carrier
transaction that commits a payload without being mined, transaction
builders with a fee loop, funding-tree state, clients for a node, an
arcade and a BRC-100 wallet, a chain tracker over a header service, host
sets with quorum fan-out, BRC-24 lookup, BRC-169 and BRC-180 resolution,
a pinned-key file, and SPV verdicts. The application supplies its own
schema, derivation, tags and wallet profile; nothing here names one.

A TypeScript package under ts/, @lightwebinc/bcommon, carries the twins
of the parts an overlay topic manager or lookup service needs: the codec,
store references, the reader's key derivation, field signatures, the
funding decode and the carrier check, plus the engine interfaces a module
satisfies and helpers for its tests.

